#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is a file manager for &kde; which aims to improve usability at the "
"user interface level. &dolphin; is not intended to be a competitor to "
"&konqueror;, &kde;'s default file manager. &dolphin; focuses only on being a "
"file manager whereas &konqueror; is a universal viewer of many file types. "
"This development approach allows for concentrating on optimizing the user "
"interface for the specific task of file management."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is currently in beta stage, but already provides most features "
"necessary for daily usage. Please report any problems or feature requests to "
"the &dolphin; author via the bug report dialog. This is accessible from the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Help</guimenu><guimenuitem>Report Bug...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> menu of the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; does not represent a wild departure from the &konqueror; file "
"manager interface. There are certain paradigms in use however, which may "
"require some readjustment on the user's part. An attempt is made below to "
"explain these in an effort to provide a more enjoyable experience for our "
"users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; User Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default &dolphin; interface consists of a (1) menu bar, (2) toolbar, (3) "
"location bar, (4) workspace and (5) status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:158 index.docbook:215 index.docbook:237 index.docbook:263
#: index.docbook:305 index.docbook:322 index.docbook:353 index.docbook:375
#: index.docbook:393 index.docbook:411 index.docbook:437 index.docbook:471
#: index.docbook:517 index.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &dolphin;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The location bar displays the path to the current folder. The location bar "
"has two versions. There is the typical line input version which shows the "
"path to the current folder via a string of text &eg; <filename class="
"\"directory\">/home/peter/Documents/</filename>. The second version of the "
"location bar uses the 'bread crumb' display. The bread crumb display makes "
"each folder a link which can be used to, immediately go to the entry. The "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/home/peter/Documents</filename> entry in the "
"bread crumb view would become 'Home > peter > Documents' with Home, peter, "
"and Documents being clickable links which are able go to there respective "
"locations. This makes navigation to folders above the current folder easier "
"and more intuitive. It also removes the need for the <guiicon>Up</guiicon> "
"icon to be present in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The workspace shows the contents of the current folder. The workspace can "
"also be configured to show the contents of a folder with multiple views. "
"More information about the workspace is provided in the following section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The status bar shows a limited amount of data relating to the file hovered "
"over and the current folder. When a file is hovered over, the status bar "
"shows the file name, the filesize and the file type &eg; JPEG. When no file "
"has been highlighted or hovered over, the status bar shows the amount of "
"files and folders in the current folder. At all times the status bar shows "
"the amount of storage space that has currently been used on the current "
"mount point, as well as the maximum space available on the mount point &eg; "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/home/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Workspace"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &dolphin; workspace can display the contents of a folder in a variety of "
"views. Currently there are icons, details and previews modes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Icons</guibutton> view shows the contents of the folder via "
"the file icon type &eg; an <acronym>MP3</acronym> file will be represented "
"with the icon for an <acronym>MP3</acronym> file. Sub-folders are "
"represented in the form of a folder icon. The folder icon is defined by the "
"&kde; icon theme currently in use, however individual folders can have their "
"icon changed manually if the user wishes. This can be done via the "
"properties dialogue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Details</guibutton> view lists the contents of a folder in "
"alphabetical order and by type. Sub-folders are at the top of the list in "
"alphabetical order, while underneath, the files within the folder are in "
"alphabetical order."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Details are displayed to the right of the files within the folder. The "
"default &dolphin; configuration only displays the size of the file and the "
"date it was last modified. More details can be added via the Configure "
"&dolphin; dialog however."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Preview</guibutton> view is similar to the icons view. The "
"difference is that wherever possible previews of the files are shown. This "
"function works for a number of image types including; JPG, PNG, XCF, "
"<acronym>SVG</acronym> and numerous others. The previews view is also "
"capable of showing the first 14 lines from text documents. &dolphin; is also "
"capable of displaying a preview of HTML and <acronym>PDF</acronym> files in "
"the previews view. It is also possible to modify the size of the previews "
"via the Configure &dolphin; dialogue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changing the view of the folder a user is working in is as simple as "
"clicking the icon of the view they wish to use. This will cause the "
"workspace view to change accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Workspace View Buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The workspace in &dolphin; is capable of showing two folders within the same "
"window, known as split workspaces. In order to enable or disable the split "
"workspace mode toggle the icon on the taskbar. Another way to enable or "
"disable the split workspace mode is to use the <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Split View</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled then the workspace will split apart. Two separate "
"workspace areas will be available for use, along with two separate location "
"bars. Clicking on either workspace will make it the active workspace. If the "
"user toggles the split workspace mode off, then the currently active "
"workspace will remain, while the inactive workspace will close."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; In Split Workspace Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of remembering the workspace view on a per-folder "
"basis. For example, if while viewing <filename class=\"directory\">/home/"
"peter/Pictures/</filename> the user choses to use the preview view, then the "
"next time the user enters that folder, the view will be changed to the "
"preview view. This is especially useful for folders containing mainly "
"images. The feature only works for local folders which the user has read/"
"write permissions to. &dolphin; will also remember the viewing mode it was "
"in when last running &eg; single workspace or split workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; can also display files and sub-folders that are hidden in the the "
"current folder &eg; files such as <filename>.dolphin</filename> and sub-"
"folder such as <filename class=\"directory\">.kde/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hidden files and sub-folders can be distinguished from non-hidden file and "
"sub-folders by their colouring. Hidden files/sub-folders are fainter then "
"non-hidden files/sub-folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Showing Hidden Files/Sub-folders Enabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To enable the showing of hidden files and sub-folders you can select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Hidden Files</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is able to sort the contents of a folder in a number of ways. "
"These are; By Name, By Date, By Size and Descending order. These only apply "
"to the current folder the user is currently in and do not affect other "
"folders. As with the Views Modes the Sorting order is saved for this folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the way the folder is sorted, via the menu "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guisubmenu>Sort By</guisubmenu></"
"menuchoice> (&eg; By Date)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &dolphin; sidebar has two modes. The first mode is the Bookmarks mode. "
"The second mode is the Information mode. The sidebar can be enabed and "
"disabled via the the menu bar; Views > Sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The sidebar mode can be changed via the drop down menu at the top. Selecting "
"Bookmarks will enable the bookmarks mode, while selecting Information will "
"enable the Information mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Bookmarks sidebar mode displays the filesystem bookmarks the user has "
"stored. The bookmarks sidebar mode also allows the user to add more "
"bookamrks, this can be done via right clicking the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Showing The Sidebar With The Bookmarks Mode Enabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Information sidebar mode also allows the user access to their service "
"menus for a given file type. A service menu entry that is directly under the "
"Actions > ... menu is diaplayed as a single button. However if a service "
"menu entry is in a submenu under the Actions > .... menu &eg; Actions > "
"Amarok, then this is presented as a drop down menu containing the options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Showing The Sidebar With The Information Mode Enabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &dolphin;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Navigation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main feature of &dolphin; that allows navigation of the file system is "
"the work space. Clicking on a sub-folder within the current folder changes "
"to this folder. Clicking on files within the workspace will open the file in "
"the default application that has been assigned to it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tool bar is also used for navigating the file system. The tool bar "
"contains two buttons essential for navigating the file system quickly and "
"easily, these are; <guiicon>Back</guiicon> and <guiicon>Forward</guiicon>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:359
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Toolbar Buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Other buttons can be added to the toolbar to further aid navigation or to "
"provide short cuts for functions within &dolphin; &eg; deleting a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; continually shows the folder that it is currently viewing the "
"contents of, via the location bar and the title bar. The location bar has "
"two views available. The first is the folder path view. This shows the path "
"to the current folder &eg; <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share/apps/"
"dolphin/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Displaying The Folder Path View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The second view is the breadcrumb view. This allows the user to move to a "
"folder a number of folders back from the current one. This is achieved via a "
"tab like interface where the name of each previous folder is displayed and "
"can be clicked on to change into."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Displaying The Breadcrumb View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to change between the two location bar views, click on the the "
"browse button. This will toggle the view between the folder path view and "
"the bread crumb view. A second way of switching between the folder path view "
"and the breadcrumb view is via <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu> "
"<guisubmenu>Navigation Bar</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Edit Location</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Browse Button"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With the folder path view the user is able to enter the whole path to the "
"folder they wish to enter. In order to do so, the user can toggle the browse "
"button to the folder path view or alternatively via the menu <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Navigation Bar</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Edit Location</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> then enter the path "
"to the folder they wish to enter. The user will notice as they are entering "
"the path, a box will open underneath the address bar showing the content of "
"the folder they are currently heading to. The content of this box will "
"change as they continue to enter the path to the folder, showing the folders "
"and the files beginning with the characters being entered &eg; <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/apps/k</filename> would display everything "
"within the folder beginning with the k character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the breadcrumb view is enabled then the user is unable to enter the path "
"to the folder. The user must manually navigate the file system by clicking "
"the folders and sub-folders within the folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to aid the navigation of the file system, &dolphin; can use "
"bookmarks. Bookmarks can be set for any location on the filesystem including "
"virtual folders that do not physically exist, but &kde; creates for ease of "
"use &eg; trash:/. This in turn means that if the user chooses a bookmark "
"from the list the workspace will move into that folder or virtual location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Bookmark Button Open"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to select a bookmark, the location bar must be set to the "
"breadcrumb view. Clicking the image of the home button (as set by the icon "
"theme currently in use) will drop down a list of all the available "
"bookmarks. The &dolphin; sidebar also contains a bookmark list. This can be "
"accessed via switching the the sideba to bookmarks mode. The user then "
"clicks the desired bookmark to open that folder. By default &dolphin; sets "
"bookmarks for; the users home folder <filename class=\"directory\">/home/"
"username/</filename>, the Root partition and the system:/ area (location "
"were the user is able to view the storage devices). More bookmarks can be "
"set via the Configure &dolphin; dialogue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Storage Media Navigation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is not restricted to navigating your local file system, it is also "
"capable of navigating Removable Storage Media. In addition to this, "
"&dolphin; also has the ability to mount and un-mount storage media on the "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When in the &kde; folder for storage Media; system:/media/ the available "
"Storage Media are shown. Typically this is the hard drive(s)/partitions and "
"Floppy Drive. Each device is named according to their name or device type. "
"The root Partition/Drive is named / while the home partition is named /home, "
"the Floppy Disk is named Floppy Drive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Displaying The System:/Media Folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the user has inserted Removable Storage media &eg; a Flash USB disk, then "
"this will be shown. This also applies to CDROM/DVDROM drives. As with the "
"Hard Disks these devices will also be named accordingly, either by there "
"drive name, device type or in the case of CDROMS/DVDROMS by their disk name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each device found in this location has the appropriate icon for their device "
"type. However this only applies if the hal daemon is running."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; can mount devices found in the System:/media/ folder via a number "
"of ways. Firstly right clicking on the device and via the menu "
"Actions>Mount. The second way is by clicking on the device icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To un-mount a device right click on the device and via the menu; "
"Actions>Safely Remove. This will then un-mount the device."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open a mounted device there are two methods. Firstly clicking the mounted "
"device will change into that folder. The second method is by right clicking "
"the device and via the menu Actions>Open Device."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to configure &dolphin; the user needs to access the &dolphin; "
"Configuration dialogue. This can be accessed via the menu bar; <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &dolphin;...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &dolphin; Configuration dialogue consists of three sections; Startup, "
"View Modes, and General. Clicking one of these sections will make those "
"options available accordingly. The options available are displayed to the "
"right of the dialogue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Configuration Window Showing The General Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The General option allows users to set a number of options for &dolphin;, "
"these are; the default home location for the user &eg; /home/Peter, the "
"default view mode (all folders will use this view unless they have already "
"been changed) and wether or not split view is anable by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "&dolphin; Configuration Window Showing The View Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The View Modes option differes slightly from the General option in that it "
"has three tabs in the options. The Icons tab allows users to set options to "
"do with the Icons View Mode &eg; icon size. The Details tab allows users to "
"set options relating to the Details View Mode &eg; what information about "
"files are shown. The Previews to allows users to set options relating to the "
"Prevews View Mode &eg; the size of the preview images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following are a number of tips to save time when using &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Bookmarking"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To quickly create a bookmark of the folder currently being viewed, right "
"click in the work space and via the menu select Bookmark this folder. The "
"Bookmarking dialogue will open, enter a name for the bookmark along with an "
"icon to represent the bookmark."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another method is to have the sidebar enabled in the bookmarks mode. Right "
"clicking the side bar and selecting 'Add Bookmark...' will open the dialogue "
"to add bookmarks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finding Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of searching for files in a filesystem. If <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo> is pressed or using "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Find File...</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, <application>KFind</application> will open "
"already set up to search within the current folder and any sub-folders "
"contained within."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mounting Storage Media"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A quick way to mount Storage Media is to click on the device. This will "
"mount and open the device in &dolphin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open A Terminal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; can open a terminal already in the current folder. This can be "
"done by pressing the <keycap>F4</keycap> button. For example if the user "
"were in <filename class=\"directory\">/home/Peter/Packages/</filename> and "
"pressed <keycap>F4</keycap> a terminal will open already in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/home/Peter/Packages/</filename> folder or using "
"<menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Panels</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Terminal</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:599
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of undoing changes users have made to files. For "
"example if a user sent a file to the Trash, &dolphin; can undo this and move "
"it back to the folder it previously belonged in. To undo an action via the "
"menu <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Undo: (action name)</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>, &eg; <guilabel>Undo: Rename</guilabel> or by "
"pressing <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:605
#, no-c-format
msgid "Renaming A Batch Of Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of renaming a number of files at the same time. Each "
"file will have the file name specified, followed by a number for how many "
"files that have been chosen to rename &eg; Tester 1.png, Tester 2.png, "
"Tester 3.png. This is useful for when you have a number of audio files where "
"you wish to number them via their track number, or for photographs taken "
"from a digital camera."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user wishes to rename a batch of files they must first select the files "
"to be renamed. This can be done via dragging the mouse over the files to be "
"renamed, or via holding &Ctrl; and clicking each file to be renamed. The "
"user must then open the batch-rename dialogue, this, can be done via "
"pressing <keycap>F2</keycap> or via the File menu; <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Rename...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user must then enter the name they wish to give the files. The # "
"character must also be present within the name (failure to include the # key "
"will result in an error as this indicates where the file number should be "
"sequentially increased for each file.) The files will then be renamed with a "
"number present within the file name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comparing A Selection Of Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of comparing a selection of files to see the "
"differences between them. For a user to be able to compare files then the "
"<application>Kompare</application> application must be installed. &dolphin; "
"can only compare the files that <application>Kompare</application> is "
"capable on analyzing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user wishes to compare a selection of files, then first they must "
"select the files to be compared. Then launch the <application>Kompare</"
"application> application via the Tools menu; <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Compare Files</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. "
"<application>Kompare</application> will then open showing the differences "
"between the files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filter A Selection Of Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&dolphin; is capable of filtering a selection of files within the workspace "
"via a text string. For example if a user wish to filter all of the "
"<acronym>MP3</acronym> files within a folder, they could filter for .mp3. "
"This would then filter out all of the files that did not have .mp3 within "
"their file name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user wishes to filter a selection of files this can be done via the "
"filter bar. The user then enters the text they wish to filter for within "
"that folder. To enable the filter bar the user must press either the "
"<keycap>/</keycap> key or via the Menu Bar; <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Filter Bar</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>. To "
"disable the filter bar the user must press either the <keycap>Esc</keycap> "
"Key, or via the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show "
"Filter Bar</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

